DOSBox for WarpOS with MiniGL Voodoo
====================================

Build (Linux host)
------------------

    make -f makefile.wos_gcc            # G4 (-mcpu=7400)
    make -f makefile.wos_gcc CPU=604e   # 604e cards

Needs the adtools ppc-amigaos-gcc 8.4 toolchain, the MOS2WOS WarpOS SDK and
the MiniGL V19 SDK; the paths come from $(MGL_DIR)/Makefile.wos.gcc.common
(override MGL_DIR, WOS_TOOLCHAIN_BIN, MOS2WOS_ROOT as needed). The result is
wos_objs/dosbox.warpelf, an ET_REL object that the link step has already
checked against the Elf2Exe2 contract (no undefined/COMMON symbols, only
ADDR32/ADDR16_LO/ADDR16_HA/REL24 relocations, _start at .text+0).

Build notes
-----------

- No C++ exceptions: the SDK's libstdc++/libgcc unwind tables use R_PPC_REL32,
  which Elf2Exe2 rejects, so .eh_frame is discarded and the sources are
  compiled with -fno-exceptions. E_Exit and the quit paths longjmp back to
  main() instead (C_NO_EXCEPTIONS in config.h, include/dosbox.h).
- The C++ COMDAT section groups are stripped (objcopy -R .group) from every
  object and from a copy of libstdc++.a: binutils 2.23 keeps them as
  thousands of separate sections in a relocatable link.
- Frontend is src/gui/sdlmain.cpp, but SDL is used for audio only. The
  screen and input are native (src/platform/warpos/wos_video.c): a 15/16-bit
  RTG screen of at least 640x480 (fullresolution sets a larger one), the
  changed rows copied under one LockBitMapTagList per frame, and a backdrop
  window polled with one SetSignal. Measured with SDL's video, SDL's event
  pump (GetMsg plus a lowlevel joystick read, 3.5-4 ms) and surface updates
  took most of the PPC's time. Always full screen; no key mapper editor
  (bindings still load from the mapper file); no joystick yet.
- No OpenGL output, no SDL_sound (CD audio from cue/bin images plays raw BIN
  tracks only, no WAV/MP3/OGG tracks), no IPX or modem networking yet.
- The SDK's bits/gthr-default.h does not match its libstdc++.a (64- vs
  60-byte mutex): src/platform/warpos/include/bits/gthr-default.h overrides
  it. Without it the first std::ifstream crashes in std::locale::operator=.
- Profiling: SetEnv WOS_PROF 1 appends a line every 5 s to T:dbprof.txt
  with the share of time in the CPU core, PIC events, event polling, tick
  handling and frame updates, plus frames and the auto cycle count.
- Disk images (imgmount) are read a sector per dos.library call and are
  slow; mount the game's files as a drawer when possible.
- src/platform/warpos/wos_runtime.c stubs the libitm symbols libstdc++
  references weakly; nothing in DOSBox can reach them.

Install
-------

On the Amiga, convert the object once per build:

    Stack 100000
    Elf2Exe2 dosbox.warpelf DOSBoxWOS

Put DOSBoxWOS, the matched minigl_ppc.dll and dosbox.conf in one drawer.
The configuration is read from that drawer (PROGDIR:dosbox.conf); mount
AmigaDOS paths as usual, e.g. "mount c DH1:dos" or "mount d PROGDIR:games".

Run
---

Put minigl_ppc_host and the DOSBox-WOS script (src/platform/warpos/) in the
drawer too. Run C:InitPPC once per boot if your WarpOS setup needs it, then:

    CD Work:DOSBox
    Execute DOSBox-WOS [dosbox arguments]

The script sets the MGLPPC_* environment of the Quake3-R200 release, starts
minigl_ppc_host in the background (it stays running and is reused) and runs
DOSBoxWOS with a 1 MB stack. MINIGL_CTILE is not set: LFB reads use
glReadPixels, which a tiled render target would scramble.

[voodoo] settings
-----------------

    voodoo_card=auto            ; false, software, minigl, auto (= minigl)
    voodoo_memsize=4            ; 4 (one TMU) or 12 (two TMUs)
    voodoo_minigl_fullscreen=true
    voodoo_minigl_depth=16      ; 16 or 32

The emulated card is a Voodoo Graphics (SST-1) on the PCI bus with its LFB
at 0xD0000000; DOS Glide 2.x games find it as usual. With minigl the 3D
output opens a MiniGL screen when a game enables the Voodoo display and
closes it when the game switches back to VGA. If MiniGLOpen() fails (DLL
missing, host not running) DOSBox logs it and falls back to software
rendering through the normal DOSBox window.

While the MiniGL screen is up, keyboard and mouse are read from the MiniGL
window directly (the DOSBox key mapper is bypassed); Ctrl+F9 quits.

Known limits of the MiniGL backend
----------------------------------

- SST-1 colour/alpha/texture combine units are mapped onto fixed-function
  GL_MODULATE/GL_DECAL with per-vertex colours. Uncommon combiner modes
  (subtract-and-add forms, local-select override, detail/LOD blending)
  are approximated.
- Fog is applied to vertex colours: exact for black fog and untextured
  polygons, approximate for coloured fog on textured polygons.
- No mipmaps; textures are uploaded at their base LOD.
- LFB writes in accelerated mode are drawn as GL points and LFB reads use
  glReadPixels; games that stream full frames through the LFB are slow.
  Use voodoo_card=software for those.
- Perspective-correct texturing relies on homogeneous vertices; whether the
  R200 path interpolates perspective-correctly depends on the MiniGL backend.
